1 bank on: \begin{align*}
\binom{8}{1}+\binom{8}{3}+\binom{8}{5}+\binom{8}{7}&=8+56+56+70=200
\end{align*}

2 banks on: \begin{align*}
\binom{8}{2}+\binom{8}{4}+\binom{8}{6}+\binom{8}{8}&=28+56+56+1=141
\end{align*}

Thus, there are $\boxed{200+141=341}$ ways to set the switches so that either one or two banks of lights are on.

