\cos (\pi v) &= \sqrt{1-v^2}
\end{align*}
Solving for $u$ in the first equation, we get $u = \sin (\pi u) / \sqrt{1-\sin^2(\pi u)}$. Substituting this into the second equation, we have
\begin{align*}
