The function $f(x)$ is even, so $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x$. The function $g(x)$ is odd, so $g(-x)=-g(x)$ for all $x$. Thus, for all $x$,
\begin{align*}
f(-x)g(-x) &= f(x) (-g(x)) \\
&= (-f(x))g(x) \neq f(x)g(x)
\end{align*}
Therefore, $f(x)g(x)$ is not even, not odd, so $f(x)g(x)$ is neither even nor odd.

