The determinant given is a Vandermonde determinant. We can factor it as follows:
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} &= (a + x)^3 - 3(a - x)^3 \\
&= (a + x - a + x)^3 - 3(a - x - a + x)^3 \\
&= (2x)^3 - 3(2x)^3 \\
&= -2x^3.
\end{align*}
Setting this equal to zero, we find that $x = 0$ is a solution.

For $x \neq 0$, we can rewrite the determinant as
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} &= -2x^3(1 - x^2) \\
&= -2x^3(1 - a^2/x^2).
\end{align*}
Since the determinant is zero, we have $1 - a^2/x^2 = 0$, so $a^2 = x^2$. We can then find two possible values for $x$: $\pm \sqrt{a^2}$, so the possible values for $x$ are $\boxed{a}$ and $\boxed{-a}$.

