f(x) &= x^2+2x-3 \\
&= (x+1)^2+(-4) \\
&= (x+1+2i)(x+1-2i) - 4.
\end{align*}
The $x$-coordinate of the vertex is the average of the $x$-intercepts, which are $-1+2i$ and $-1-2i$. The average is $-1$, and the $y$-coordinate of the vertex is the negative of the leading coefficient, which is $-4$. Therefore, the vertex is at $(-1,-4)$, and the maximum value of $f(x)$ is $f(-1)=-4$.

