The least common multiple is the smallest number that is a multiple of both numbers. We can use prime factorization to find the LCM.
\begin{align*}
12 &= 2^2 \cdot 3 \\
18 &= 2^2 \cdot 3 \cdot 3
\end{align*}
Since $12$ and $18$ have the same prime factors (just with different powers), the LCM is $2^2 \cdot 3^2 = \boxed{36}$.

